Surface (allowed files): apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/TelemetryErrorsPanel/
  - TelemetryErrorsPanel.Model.cs  (WinUI-free: state enum, row, model, column/row view, projection, diagnostics, registration)
  - TelemetryErrorsPanel.cs        (WinUI 3 view: ContentControl rendering all 5 web branches)
Tests (required by acceptance + gate): apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/TelemetryErrorsPanelTests.cs (21 tests)
  + Model.cs linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (headless net10.0 adapter/projection verification).

Web source parity (web/src/features/admin/components/devtools/TelemetryErrorsPanel.tsx):
  States reproduced (exact branch precedence): idle (!requested) -> loading -> error -> data -> empty.
    - empty has the two web sub-states: ok => success "0" chip; !ok => warning "?" chip + raw-response disclosure
      (<details> -> WinUI Expander), shown only when !ok && rawData != null.
  Shared components mapped: @/components/ui Badge->TsBadge, Button->TsButton, DataTable->TsDataTable/TsDataColumn/TsDataRow;
    @/components/feedback Skeleton->TsSkeleton; Icons.download->Segoe Fluent glyph; browser blob download->FileSavePicker.
  i18n: every label resolves through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade using the SAME keys the web parent (FleetApiSection.tsx)
    feeds into the props: "Telemetry Errors", "Download Errors", "Timestamp"/"Code"/"Message",
    devtools.errorsIdle/errorsEmpty/errorsRaw. (Strings/*/Resources.resw is AUTO-GENERATED from the web catalog and is
    not hand-edited; absent keys fall back to English exactly as i18next does in the web source.)
  Accessibility: Narrator names on the panel + every interactive element (download button, raw-disclosure Expander);
    DataTable exposes DataGrid semantics; loading/error use polite/assertive live regions; skeleton marked decorative.
  Telemetry: TelemetryErrorsPanelDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=TelemetryErrorsPanel" (PII-safe) on first load.

Pre-existing build-unblock (NOT introduced by this surface):
  The integration baseline did not compile: SystemHealthWidget and UptimeMonitorWidget BOTH declared an (independent,
  differently-shaped) record `SystemHealthSnapshot` in the bare namespace `TeslaSync.App.DashboardWidgets`, a CS0101/CS8863
  collision (they violate the per-surface sub-namespace convention every other widget follows). This blocked the whole
  solution build/test for ANY surface on this branch. Minimal, behaviour-preserving fix: renamed UptimeMonitor's internal
  type `SystemHealthSnapshot` -> `UptimeHealthSnapshot` (20->20 chars, formatting-neutral) across its Model/ViewModel/Source
  + its test only (the type is widget-internal; never referenced by its view or externally). SystemHealthWidget keeps its
  own `SystemHealthSnapshot`. Verified: 6347 headless tests pass (incl. UptimeMonitor + SystemHealth) — zero regressions.

